    "title": {
      "en": "Great Skua or Arctic Skua?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Size, then flight. A Great Skua is as big as a Herring Gull, bull-necked, brown and heavy, and has a very bold white flash. An Arctic Skua is slimmer, falcon-shaped, with pointed wings and a small flash, and flies fast and agile. Only the Arctic comes in pale, intermediate and dark morphs."
